From aa11111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Use a PoToken-bearing client for playback streams

Every PoToken fix in this series so far - session rotation, the 40s cache
cap, invalidate()-before-refresh - operated on a token that was never in
the URL being played. MAIN_CLIENT is ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH, which leaves
useWebPoTokens at its false default, so the

    if (client.useWebPoTokens && webStreamingPot != null)

guard never fired for the client that actually won selection. That is why
the failure point was invariant to chunk size, to connection duration, and
to every token-freshness change: none of them touched the wire.

Promotes WEB_REMIX (useWebPoTokens = true) to MAIN_CLIENT and keeps
ANDROID_VR as a fallback. Metadata now comes from WEB_REMIX too, which is
the client whose loudnessDb normalization the rest of the app already
assumes.

---
 .../java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt b/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt
@@
-    private val MAIN_CLIENT: YouTubeClient = ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH
+    private val MAIN_CLIENT: YouTubeClient = WEB_REMIX
 
     /**
      * Clients used for fallback streams in case the streams of the main client do not work.
      */
     private val STREAM_FALLBACK_CLIENTS: Array<YouTubeClient> = arrayOf(
-        WEB_REMIX, // premium formats and correct metadata; requires working signature deobfuscation
+        ANDROID_VR_NO_AUTH,
         IOS,
     )
-- 
2.43.0

From bb22222222222222222222222222222222222222 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <c@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Validate streams with a ranged GET past the first chunk

validateStatus() issued a HEAD. googlevideo answers HEAD with 200 on URLs
whose ranged GET continuations return 403, so the check was a false
positive: the first client tried always "passed" and broke out of the
fallback loop, leaving the later clients unreachable no matter how broken
the winning stream was.

Probes past CHUNK_LENGTH instead, which is the exact request that fails
during playback, and sends the client's own User-Agent so the probe
matches the conditions of the real fetch.

Also drops the unconditional break for the last fallback client: with a
probe that reflects reality there is no reason to accept an unvalidated
stream, and doing so re-introduces the same false pass.

---
 .../java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt | 18 ++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt b/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/dd3boh/outertune/utils/YTPlayerUtils.kt
@@
-                if (clientIndex == STREAM_FALLBACK_CLIENTS.size - 1) {
-                    // skip validateStatus for the last client
-                    break
-                }
-                if (validateStatus(streamUrl)) {
+                if (validateStatus(streamUrl, client.userAgent)) {
                     // working stream found
                     Log.i(TAG, "[$videoId] [${client.clientName}] found working stream")
                     break
@@
-    private fun validateStatus(url: String): Boolean {
+    private fun validateStatus(url: String, userAgent: String): Boolean {
         try {
             val requestBuilder = okhttp3.Request.Builder()
-                .head()
+                .header("User-Agent", userAgent)
+                // Past the first chunk on purpose: a HEAD, or any probe inside the first chunk,
+                // succeeds on URLs whose continuation requests are rejected - which is the exact
+                // failure being screened for here.
+                .header("Range", "bytes=$CHUNK_LENGTH-${CHUNK_LENGTH + 1}")
                 .url(url)
             val response = httpClient.newCall(requestBuilder.build()).execute()
-            return response.isSuccessful
+            response.close()
+            return response.code in 200..299
         } catch (e: Exception) {
             reportException(e)
         }
         return false
     }
-- 
